WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.220
DNA is a polymer: a long chain built
from small units called nucleotides.

2
00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:10.460
It has two strands, twisted
together into a double helix.

3
00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:14.160
Across the middle, the
bases pair: A with T,

4
00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:15.760
G with C.

5
00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:20.890
Each pair is held by hydrogen bonds,
and one hydrogen bond is weak.

6
00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:24.010
So if only weak bonds
join the two strands,

7
00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:26.520
why doesn't DNA fall apart?

8
00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:29.930
In this mission, you'll build
a nucleotide from three parts,

9
00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:33.120
then link nucleotides into a strand.

10
00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:36.090
Then you'll pair two
strands, base by base,

11
00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:38.350
and twist them into a helix.

12
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:42.810
Your mission: explain why DNA's
two strands stay together,

13
00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:44.830
though only weak bonds join them.
